  "profiling_caveats": "Public pstats StatsProfile times round to milliseconds and instrumentation slows deepcopy; fraction describes that profile, not uninstrumented dispatch latency. Stage listener counts calls, profile listener is a no-op. tracemalloc is Python allocation only, not native/whole-app RSS. Unpinned CPU/background load, one Windows run; no latency SLO or cross-hardware/floor promise.",
  "decision": "Keep snapshot/alias safety. Existing short-history costs and JSON vs render boundaries are now measured; no immutable/zero-copy/checkpoint rewrite, validation removal, long-history/concurrency optimization is justified by these snapshots alone.",
  "initial_qa_failure": "The first private run used non-exported mp.SetTitle; it failed before measurement, was not a product bug and is not counted as successful data. The script now uses existing mp.actions.",
